{
  "computation_method": {
    "name": "rescue_eta_v1",
    "description": "Rescue ETA is not a raw measured field — it is a derived value computed at query time from facility/incident coordinates and the site's mapped trail geometry.",
    "steps": [
      "1. straight_line_distance_m = haversine(facility.lat, facility.lon, incident.lat, incident.lon)",
      "2. trail_correction_factor = trail_path_length / straight_line_endpoint_distance, derived from the two mapped trail segments (P1, P2) in the KML — accounts for switchbacks vs as-the-crow-flies",
      "3. estimated_path_distance_m = straight_line_distance_m * trail_correction_factor",
      "4. elevation_gain_m = incident.altitude_m - facility.altitude_m (clamped at 0 if descending)",
      "5. eta_min = (estimated_path_distance_m / 1000 / base_speed_kmh * 60) + (elevation_gain_m / 100 * naismith_climb_min_per_100m)"
    ],
    "constants": {
      "base_speed_kmh": 4.5,
      "naismith_climb_min_per_100m": 10,
      "trail_correction_factor_derivation": {
        "P1_segment": { "name": "Parking access trail", "mapped_length_m": 554.3, "straight_line_endpoints_m": 517.5, "ratio": 1.071 },
        "P2_segment": { "name": "Watchtower approach trail", "mapped_length_m": 351.7, "straight_line_endpoints_m": 319.4, "ratio": 1.101 },
        "trail_correction_factor_used": 1.09,
        "note": "Average of the two mapped ratios. Applied uniformly since no trail geometry exists for the other facility-incident pairs; treat as an estimate, not surveyed distance."
      }
    },
    "caveats": [
      "Straight-line + correction-factor approach, not a routed shortest-path over the actual trail network — only two short trail segments (P1, P2) are digitized in the source KML.",
      "Does not account for terrain difficulty, water crossings, or the source KML's own note that the plunge pool boundary and stream centreline are unverified estimates.",
      "Assumes on-foot travel only; does not model vehicle access from the railway station or boat/vehicle rescue options."
    ]
  },

